(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain File Handling in Python. Detail open\(\) modes \('r', 'w', 'a', 'x', '+', 'b'\), buffer flushing, and why Context Managers \(with\) are mandatory in production.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of File I/O:) Tj
T*
(   File I/O enables persistent data storage on non-volatile secondary media.) Tj
T*
(   In Python, file interaction follows a strict three-phase lifecycle:) Tj
T*
(   1. Open Stream: Binding a file path to an OS file descriptor via open\(\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Read/Write Operations: Transferring byte/character streams between system memory and storage) Tj
T*
(   buffers.) Tj
T*
(   3. Close Stream: Flushing memory buffers and releasing the file descriptor back to the) Tj
T*
(   operating system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comprehensive File Mode Inventory:) Tj
T*
(   - 'r': Read-only \(Default\). File must exist; otherwise raises FileNotFoundError. Pointer at) Tj
T*
(   start.) Tj
T*
(   - 'w': Write-only. Creates file if missing; TRUNCATES existing file to 0 bytes! Pointer at) Tj
T*
(   start.) Tj
T*
(   - 'a': Append. Creates file if missing. Writes ALWAYS append to the end of file.) Tj
T*
(   - 'x': Exclusive creation. Creates file; raises FileExistsError if file already exists.) Tj
T*
(   - 'b': Binary mode \(rb, wb, ab\). Reads/writes raw bytes \(bytes\) without character decoding.) Tj
T*
(   - 't': Text mode \(Default\). Handles encoding/decoding \(UTF-8\) and newline translations.) Tj
T*
(   - '+': Update mode \(r+, w+, a+\). Opens file for simultaneous reading and writing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The with Statement \(Context Manager\):) Tj
T*
(   Failing to close files causes File Descriptor Leaks. In long-running servers, exhausting) Tj
T*
(   available file descriptors causes all subsequent file and socket operations to crash.) Tj
T*
(   The with statement implements the Context Manager Protocol \(__enter__ and __exit__\). It) Tj
T*
(   guarantees that the file stream is flushed and closed when execution leaves the block, even) Tj
T*
(   during unexpected exceptions!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import os) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def file_io_demonstration\(filename="audit_log.txt"\):) Tj
T*
(   # Safe writing via context manager) Tj
T*
(   with open\(filename, "w", encoding="utf-8"\) as f:) Tj
T*
(   f.write\("Line 1: System Boot Initialized.\\n"\)) Tj
T*
(   f.write\("Line 2: Memory Integrity Verified.\\n"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Safe appending) Tj
T*
(   with open\(filename, "a", encoding="utf-8"\) as f:) Tj
T*
(   f.write\("Line 3: Service Worker Online.\\n"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Reading via line-by-line generator iteration) Tj
T*
(   print\("Reading file line-by-line:"\)) Tj
T*
(   with open\(filename, "r", encoding="utf-8"\) as f:) Tj
T*
(   for line_num, line in enumerate\(f, start=1\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" [{line_num}] {line.strip\(\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Is file closed after with block? {f.closed}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
