(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the os and os.path Modules in Python. Demonstrate directory navigation, directory creation, path joining, listing, file metadata, and shutil operations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundations of Filesystem Operations:) Tj
T*
(   The os and os.path modules provide cross-platform abstractions over operating system filesystem) Tj
T*
(   APIs:) Tj
T*
(   - Path Normalization: os.path.join\('a', 'b'\) uses backslashes on Windows \('a\\\\b'\) and forward) Tj
T*
(   slashes on POSIX \('a/b'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inspection: os.path.exists\(\), os.path.isfile\(\), os.path.isdir\(\), os.path.getsize\(\).) Tj
T*
(   - Directory Management: os.mkdir\(\) \(single directory\), os.makedirs\(\) \(recursive parent) Tj
T*
(   directory creation\), os.listdir\(\), os.scandir\(\).) Tj
T*
(   - High-Level Shell Utilities \(shutil\): shutil.copy2\(\) \(copies file preserving metadata\),) Tj
T*
(   shutil.move\(\), shutil.rmtree\(\) \(recursive directory deletion\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation & Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import os) Tj
T*
(   import shutil) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
