12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the re Module Architecture in Python. Detail regex compilation, pattern matching lifecycle, and compare match\(\), search\(\), findall\(\), finditer\(\), and sub\(\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture of Python's re Module:) Tj
T*
(   CPython's re module implements an interpreted bytecode regex engine based on a backtracking) Tj
T*
(   Nondeterministic Finite Automaton \(NFA\).) Tj
T*
(   Execution Pipeline:) Tj
T*
(   1. Pattern Compilation: re.compile\(regex_str, flags\) parses the string into an internal AST and) Tj
T*
(   emits optimized regex bytecode \(stored in a Pattern object\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Match Execution: The PVM regex engine runs the bytecode against target text.) Tj
T*
(   3. Match Object Generation: Returns a Match object containing match boundaries and captured) Tj
T*
(   groups.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comprehensive Method Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   - re.match\(pat, str\): Matches ONLY at index 0 \(start of string\). Returns Match or None.) Tj
T*
(   - re.search\(pat, str\): Scans the string left-to-right, returning the FIRST match found) Tj
T*
(   anywhere.) Tj
T*
(   - re.fullmatch\(pat, str\): Requires the pattern to match the ENTIRE string from start to end.) Tj
T*
(   - re.findall\(pat, str\): Returns all non-overlapping matches as a list of strings \(or tuples of) Tj
T*
(   groups\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
