(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Regular Expression Metacharacters, Quantifiers, and Character Classes in Python. Contrast Greedy versus Non-Greedy \(Lazy\) Matching with illustrative HTML parsing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Regular Expression Syntax Elements:) Tj
T*
(   - Character Classes:) Tj
T*
(   [abc]: Matches 'a', 'b', or 'c'.) Tj
T*
(   [^abc]: Negated class: matches any character EXCEPT 'a', 'b', or 'c'.) Tj
T*
(   [a-z0-9]: Range of characters.) Tj
T*
(   - Metacharacters & Special Sequences:) Tj
T*
(   \\d \(digit\), \\D \(non-digit\), \\w \(word char [a-zA-Z0-9_]\), \\W \(non-word\), \\s \(whitespace\), \\b) Tj
T*
(   \(word boundary\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Greedy versus Non-Greedy \(Lazy\) Matching:) Tj
T*
(   - Greedy Quantifiers \(*, +, {m,n}\): Match as MANY characters as possible, backing off only if) Tj
T*
(   subsequent pattern elements fail.) Tj
T*
(   - Non-Greedy / Lazy Quantifiers \(*?, +?, ??, {m,n}?\): Match as FEW characters as possible,) Tj
T*
(   expanding only if subsequent pattern elements fail.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

