(   3. The Classic HTML Parsing Dilemma:) Tj
T*
(   Consider parsing HTML tags in text: '<div><b>Title</b></div>' with pattern '<.*>':) Tj
T*
(   - Greedy '<.*>': Matches from the very first '<' all the way to the very last '>'!) Tj
T*
(   Result: '<div><b>Title</b></div>' \(A single massive catastrophic match!\).) Tj
T*
(   - Lazy '<.*?>': Matches from each '<' up to the nearest '>'.) Tj
T*
(   Result: '<div>', '<b>', '</b>', '</div>' \(Correctly tokenizes individual tags!\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import re) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   html_snippet = "<div><p>Paragraph 1</p><span>Caption</span></div>") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   greedy_pat = re.compile\(r'<.*>'\)) Tj
T*
(   lazy_pat = re.compile\(r'<.*?>'\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   greedy_matches = greedy_pat.findall\(html_snippet\)) Tj
T*
(   lazy_matches = lazy_pat.findall\(html_snippet\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Original HTML: '{html_snippet}'"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"\\nGreedy \(<.*>\): Matches {len\(greedy_matches\)} item: {greedy_matches}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Non-Greedy \(<.*?>\): Matches {len\(lazy_matches\)} items: {lazy_matches}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Extracting tag content via lazy capture) Tj
T*
(   content_pat = re.compile\(r'<p>\(.*?\)</p>'\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Extracted Paragraph Content: {content_pat.findall\(html_snippet\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N\) single scan; Greedy backtracking may degrade to O\(N^2\) if) Tj
T*
(   misconfigured.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(Matches\) memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
