12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Lookahead and Lookbehind Assertions \(Zero-Width Assertions\) in Python Regular Expressions: \(?=...\), \(?!...\), \(?<=...\), and \(?<!...\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis of Lookaround Assertions:) Tj
T*
(   Lookaround assertions are Zero-Width Assertions: they determine whether a subpattern can match) Tj
T*
(   immediately before or after the current position WITHOUT consuming characters or including them) Tj
T*
(   in the match result:) Tj
T*
(   1. Positive Lookahead \(?=pattern\): Asserts that pattern matches directly ahead.) Tj
T*
(   2. Negative Lookahead \(?!pattern\): Asserts that pattern does NOT match directly ahead.) Tj
T*
(   3. Positive Lookbehind \(?<=pattern\): Asserts that pattern matches directly behind \(Must be) Tj
T*
(   fixed width in standard Python re!\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Negative Lookbehind \(?<!pattern\): Asserts that pattern does NOT match directly behind.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Practical Password Policy Enforcement:) Tj
T*
(   Verify a password satisfies all corporate security requirements in a single regex:) Tj
T*
(   - At least 8 characters: .{8,}) Tj
T*
(   - At least one digit: \(?=.*\\d\)) Tj
T*
(   - At least one uppercase: \(?=.*[A-Z]\)) Tj
T*
(   - At least one special symbol: \(?=.*[!@#$%^&*]\)) Tj
T*
(   Unified Regex: ^\(?=.*[a-z]\)\(?=.*[A-Z]\)\(?=.*\\d\)\(?=.*[!@#$%^&*]\).{8,}$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation & Verification:) Tj
T*
(   import re) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   password_validator = re.compile\(r'^\(?=.*[a-z]\)\(?=.*[A-Z]\)\(?=.*\\d\)\(?=.*[!@#$%^&*]\).{8,}$'\)) Tj
T*
ET

