/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a File Deduplication and Checksum Verification Tool in Python using hashlib \(SHA-256\) and os.walk to detect identical files across directories.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of File Deduplication:) Tj
T*
(   Two files are duplicate if their cryptographic hash digests \(e.g. SHA-256\) are identical,) Tj
T*
(   regardless of filename or modification date.) Tj
T*
(   Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   1. Walk directory tree using os.walk\(\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Group files by exact byte size \(files of different sizes cannot be identical!\).) Tj
T*
(   3. For files sharing the same size, compute SHA-256 digest by streaming chunks of 64 KB to) Tj
T*
(   avoid loading large files into RAM.) Tj
T*
ET

