(   [Problem Statement]: Implement an Asynchronous Exception-Resilient Web Crawler Queue Simulation in Python with retry budgets and exponential backoff.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context:) Tj
T*
(   In distributed network scraping, transient network errors \(timeouts, rate limits\) occur) Tj
T*
(   frequently. The crawler must retry failed requests with exponential backoff before logging) Tj
T*
(   fatal failures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   import time) Tj
T*
(   import random) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class ResilientNetworkClient:) Tj
T*
(   @staticmethod) Tj
T*
(   def fetch_with_backoff\(url: str, max_retries=3, base_delay=0.1\) -> str:) Tj
T*
(   for attempt in range\(1, max_retries + 1\):) Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   # Simulate flaky network request) Tj
T*
(   if random.random\(\) < 0.6 and attempt < 3:) Tj
T*
(   raise ConnectionResetError\("Transient TCP reset"\)) Tj
T*
(   return f"200 OK: Content from {url}") Tj
T*
(   except ConnectionResetError as err:) Tj
T*
(   delay = base_delay * \(2 ** \(attempt - 1\)\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"[RETRY] Attempt {attempt} failed \({err}\). Backing off {delay:.2f}s..."\)) Tj
T*
(   time.sleep\(delay\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   raise TimeoutError\(f"Failed to fetch {url} after {max_retries} attempts."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   res = ResilientNetworkClient.fetch_with_backoff\("https://api.university.edu/data"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("Success:", res\)) Tj
T*
(   except TimeoutError as ex:) Tj
T*
(   print\("Fatal:", ex\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(Retries\) with exponential delay.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) stack memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

