BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Universal File Format Detector in Python using Magic Numbers \(File Signatures\) by inspecting the first 8 header bytes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Magic Numbers:) Tj
T*
(   Relying on file extensions \(.pdf, .png\) is unreliable and unsecure. Operating systems and) Tj
T*
(   forensic tools identify file types by reading the first few header bytes \(Magic Numbers\):) Tj
T*
(   - PDF: %PDF \(25 50 44 46\)) Tj
T*
(   - PNG: \\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n \(89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A\)) Tj
T*
(   - ZIP / JAR / DOCX: PK\\x03\\x04 \(50 4B 03 04\)) Tj
T*
(   - JPEG: \\xFF\\xD8\\xFF \(FF D8 FF\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class FileTypeDetector:) Tj
T*
(   SIGNATURES = {) Tj
T*
(   b"%PDF": "PDF Document",) Tj
T*
(   b"?PNG) Tj
T*
(   ) Tj
T*
(   ": "PNG Image",) Tj
T*
(   b"???": "JPEG Image",) Tj
T*
(   b"PK": "ZIP / Office Archive",) Tj
T*
(   b"GIF87a": "GIF Image",) Tj
T*
(   b"GIF89a": "GIF Image") Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @classmethod) Tj
T*
(   def identify\(cls, file_bytes: bytes\) -> str:) Tj
T*
(   for magic, file_type in cls.SIGNATURES.items\(\):) Tj
T*
(   if file_bytes.startswith\(magic\):) Tj
T*
(   return file_type) Tj
T*
(   return "Unknown Binary Format") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Detecting %PDF-1.4 header: -> {FileTypeDetector.identify\(b'%PDF-1.4'\)}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Detecting PNG header: -> {FileTypeDetector.identify\(b'?PNG) Tj
T*
(   ) Tj
T*
(   \\x00\\x00'\)}"\)) Tj
T*
ET

