(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Complete Email, URL, and Date Format Extractor in Python using Regular Expressions with rigorous boundary constraints.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context:) Tj
T*
(   Develop a comprehensive information extraction utility that extracts emails, valid HTTP/HTTPS) Tj
T*
(   URLs, and ISO/Standard dates \(YYYY-MM-DD or DD/MM/YYYY\) from unstructured text.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   import re) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class InformationExtractor:) Tj
T*
(   EMAIL_REGEX = re.compile\(r'[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\\.[A-Za-z]{2,}'\)) Tj
T*
(   URL_REGEX =) Tj
T*
(   re.compile\(r'https?://\(?:www\\.\)?[-a-zA-Z0-9@:%._+~#=]{1,256}\\.[a-zA-Z0-9\(\)]{1,6}[-a-zA-Z0-9\(\)@) Tj
T*
(   :%_+.~#?&/=]*'\)) Tj
T*
(   DATE_REGEX = re.compile\(r'\(?:\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}|\\d{2}/\\d{2}/\\d{4}\)'\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @classmethod) Tj
T*
(   def extract_all\(cls, text: str\) -> dict:) Tj
T*
(   return {) Tj
T*
(   "Emails": cls.EMAIL_REGEX.findall\(text\),) Tj
T*
(   "URLs": cls.URL_REGEX.findall\(text\),) Tj
T*
(   "Dates": cls.DATE_REGEX.findall\(text\)) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   corpus = """) Tj
T*
(   Published on 2026-10-26 by research team \(contact: admin@cse.university.edu\).) Tj
T*
(   For documentation, visit https://python.org or https://docs.python.org/3/.) Tj
T*
(   Next conference scheduled for 15/12/2026.) Tj
T*
(   """) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   extracted = InformationExtractor.extract_all\(corpus\)) Tj
T*
(   print\("Extracted Information Entities:"\)) Tj
T*
(   for entity_type, matches in extracted.items\(\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" {entity_type:<10}: {matches}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N\) linear sweep across text length.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(M\) extracted entity lists.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

